('rowid-12535','GHBC-REQ-012535','GS 1207:2018',17,'17.5','17.5.1','GHBC-C-003575','(2) Characteristic loads (GK, QK, WK, En, E, T) means those loads defined in Clause 17.4.1.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','16457ce09527c215d6ed3351d246016049f57cc1bc2fded9c051731f9bc78db7','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-12536','GHBC-REQ-012536','GS 1207:2018',17,'17.5','17.5.1','GHBC-C-003575','(3)  Partial safety factors to the value of loads (γf), used in design in clause 17.5.2 that takes account of the possibility of unfavourable deviations of the action values, uncertainties in modeling the effects of actions, and the significance of the particular limit state.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','3a335dc470de26021f0a030c5c5cec19599c5ee6a9c9e5aa413088e60cb04b2f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
