('rowid-12995','GHBC-REQ-012995','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.4','GHBC-C-003634','(3) Second Order Effects','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["BS 8110"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f2816f3a664a6b6889af3309234743448221846238868767238ac90aa4287b5b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-12996','GHBC-REQ-012996','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.4','GHBC-C-003634','(a) Second-order effects on storey shears and moments need not be considered when the following condition is satisfied at every floor:','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["BS 8110"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','92bcd1aef5994fcdd8c09f2c4ee2940a08fa270be0195fc2c4c088f3234061b3','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-12997','GHBC-REQ-012997','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.4','GHBC-C-003634','where   = deformability index V  = seismic design shear force acting across the storey considered','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["BS 8110"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','73c77b23b7a7597ba45a96d2e054aa93108d856e62d3de4bb7b7966c9f835f72','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-12998','GHBC-REQ-012998','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.4','GHBC-C-003634','∆el  = elastic interstorey drift due to design action K   = behaviour factor h   = floor height W  = total gravity load above the considered storey (b) The deformability index,  shall not in any case exceed the value 0.20; (c) For 0.10 <  < 0.20 second order effects shall be accounted for by means of one of the statistical methods indicated in BS 8110 (1985).','prohibited',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":0.2,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"alue 0.20; (c) For 0.10 <  < 0.20 second order effects shall be a"}]','["BS 8110"]',0.93,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','787bc684b2b847ef39ca23bc70653ff28ce301f02a0917605b97f1a7329fea35','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-12999','GHBC-REQ-012999','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(1) Modelling (a) If the building can vibrate in two orthogonal directions without significant coupling, it can be analysed by means of two separate planar models, one for each orthogonal direction (b) The condition stated in 17.10.4.2.5(1) (a) shall be assumed to occur when 17.10.4.2.1(a) (ii) is satisfied.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','899fa2823855aa46e364823786b76ab673a3fce5a0de2a62e0278d0535c23091','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13000','GHBC-REQ-013000','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(c) When 17.10.4.2.1(a)(ii) is not satisfied the model shall account for the non-planar motion of the structure (2) Modes','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','69f42d7c781865c3a7c6642ae64fa37147a8c0e36ab02545b870ab5e1f995233','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-13001','GHBC-REQ-013001','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(a) In the case of planar models, the analysis shall include for each of the two orthogonal axes at least the lowest three modes of vibration, or all modes of vibration with periods greater than 0.4 secs., whichever is greater.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":0.4,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"ion with periods greater than 0.4 secs., whichever is greater."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','5dea3bcb2eefa80c50de0f1b61900a6a3facdd98eecb5081d219301b7988a438','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13002','GHBC-REQ-013002','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(b) For non-planar models the analysis shall include for each direction of seismic action, at least four modes, two of them predominantly translational and two predominantly rotational, or all modes of vibration with periods greater than 0.4 secs., whichever is greater.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":0.4,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"ion with periods greater than 0.4 secs., whichever is greater."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','593faece493c8218aa761f80dda07560cfd97ccdc719e77f8b1ac0777a4c3537','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13003','GHBC-REQ-013003','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(c) The mode considered shall be those with the greatest participation coefficients for the direction under consideration (3) Combination of Modal Responses The response quantities (force, displacements etc) separately obtained for each mode under the effect of the design response spectrum given in Clause 17.10 5.3.4 shall be combined to obtain their corresponding design values by taking the square root of the sum of the squares of modal values.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":3.4,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"ctrum given in Clause 17.10 5.3.4 shall be combined to obtain the"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','7ef85ef1930bb25e6af7f4a61aad4ccf377fe9b8dd4c320fd550134ddc38f644','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13004','GHBC-REQ-013004','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(4) Torsional Effects (a) At each floor of the building the mass contributing to inertia forces shall be assumed to be displaced from its nominal location by the amount "0.05a‖ whichever is more unfavourable for the element to be checked, ‗a‘ being the dimension of the building in the direction orthogonal to  that of the considered seismic action.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8f707c35e284d38ea05adecf4a08f95f9043baa8e57f110870f7046591aaa8f3','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13005','GHBC-REQ-013005','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','(b) When the building is analysed by means of planar models (Clause 17.10.4.2.5 (1)), torsional effects can be accounted for by increasing the action effects due to the translational oscillations of the building by the factor  defined as:  = 1 + 0.6 x/a where x is the distance of the planar element the area of Ghana into a number of zones.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','ee0d77f85d2fd5b652bec9f5eedff41155ec836f4ddcfd9053d604df7a73d9f8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13006','GHBC-REQ-013006','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','Within each zone the normalized ground','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f6c3bba3bcbb88b72a75e1b408564df2768a8e7a8fdcadc642fe1e8bd53bb680','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13007','GHBC-REQ-013007','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','acceleration is assigned a constant value as shown in Table 17.10.5.1.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','370f0c98bce8eb8dcc5805e509c17e9355b3b686372cd6b21c49390782666b00','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13008','GHBC-REQ-013008','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.4.2.5','GHBC-C-003635','ZONES','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8c9ca5933cf83fded38e0f539d3a3178a22ab2010c882fc1698fb2b72f5be5c7','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13009','GHBC-REQ-013009','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.2','GHBC-C-003636','(1) For the purpose of the Code, the ground motion shall be adequately described by means of: (a) the peak ground acceleration Amax, treated as a random variable of known distribution;','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','59288a27d8d50ce57dc6701fe3dd8ac4d2db1c8e6558ad491a43716c3de9a1b5','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13010','GHBC-REQ-013010','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.2','GHBC-C-003636','(b) one or more response spectra for horizontal motion, having a form  appropriate for the area and firm soil conditions, normalized to Amax = 1 and probabilistically characterized; (c) one or more response spectra for vertical motion, scaled to 2/3 of the correspondence horizontal motion response spectra. d) The regional values in table 17.10.5.1 should serve as a guide only.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":5.1,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"egional values in table 17.10.5.1 should serve as a guide only."}]','[]',0.93,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','0c16ba237aaa18f6ad5d33edd8fb2d7ad5d2560957b8933c55e52e09e999f6ca','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-13011','GHBC-REQ-013011','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.2','GHBC-C-003636','The particular PGA value for a specific site should be determined from the regional values based on the geotechnical characterization of the site to recommend a specific PGA value considering sites proximity to fault line, subsoil densification (using, for example, standard penetration test values- SPT) and soil classification, groundwater conditions and the functions of the building etc. (2) For particular zones, for instance, where geological evidence indicates the possibility of ‗near field‘ type of shocks (for which the response spectrum concept is inadequate) or where there is extensive and deep soil layering (for which selective amplification can occur) the expected characteristics of ground motion shall be determined by special studies.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1c6424de812718f4b27ae5890fbf82fa6f88ee3fc7f6192e367186b61d2215e4','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13012','GHBC-REQ-013012','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.1','GHBC-C-003638','Spectrum For the purpose of this Code, the shape of the ‗standard‘ (rocky or firm soil condition) elastic response spectrum normalized to a unit peak ground acceleration shall be idealized as shown in Fig. 1.4.2.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','e54de7721b5f29e7b3a363b4eab93cb45f52e487caae2e42ae6b2a5aa0eca334','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13013','GHBC-REQ-013013','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.1','GHBC-C-003638','Spectrum','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','122372e78b7a9bc71cf5c3019e16dbd2e919c70a76ffaee2db316941ca450cba','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13014','GHBC-REQ-013014','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','When more detailed knowledge of the effects of local soil conditions and on the characteristics of ground motions arriving at the site from possibly different sources is not available the procedure in Clause 17.10.5.3.2 (1) and (2), and 17.10.4.4.3 shall be applied.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":4.3,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":".3.2 (1) and (2), and 17.10.4.4.3 shall be applied."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ba3acc5a52d6450d7d90b94966f08fc61eef9303cca98f7f9b818597d51f28df','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13015','GHBC-REQ-013015','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','(1) Soil Profile Types The effects of site conditions on building response shall be established based on the soil profile types defined as follows: i SOIL PROFILE S1: Rock of any characteristic either shale-like or crystalline (such material may be characterized by a shear wave velocity greater than 800mm/sec); or stiff soil conditions where the soil depth is less than 60m and the soil type overlying rock are stable deposits of sands gravel or stiffer clays. ii SOIL PROFILE S2: Deep cohesionless or stiff clay soil conditions, including sites where the soil depth exceeds 60m and the soil types overlying rock are stable deposits of sands, gravels or stiff clay. iii SOIL PROFILE S3: Soft-to-medium stiff clays and sands, characterized by l0m or more of soft-medium stiff clay with or without intervening layers of sand and other cohesionless soils.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"comparison","value":60,"unit":null,"operator":"less than","context":"tions where the soil depth is less than 60m and the soil type overlying "},{"parameter":"measurement","value":800,"unit":"mm","operator":null,"context":"ar wave velocity greater than 800mm/sec); or stiff soil condition"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":60,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"e the soil depth is less than 60m and the soil type overlying r"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":60,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":" where the soil depth exceeds 60m and the soil types overlying "},{"parameter":"measurement","value":0,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":" and sands, characterized by l0m or more of soft-medium stiff "}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','639e1aca2c13f9afcdc2cda30918e0a7e7b545a244eab11af37d9d445b91ed36','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13016','GHBC-REQ-013016','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','In locations where soil properties are not known in sufficient detail to determine the soil profile type or where the profile does not fit any of the three types, soil profile S2 shall be used.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":2,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"he three types, soil profile S2 shall be used."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','30244d15a2b732244ccc5e4312036cc51682ecae20b54c0427d4f7a04a9b6390','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13017','GHBC-REQ-013017','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','(2)  Site Co-efficient The site co-efficient S is used to modify the standard elastic response spectrum to account for the site condition.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','da89151b6b21d16aba38218601252c9eb7c043f904989539b34f0cc504706b57','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13018','GHBC-REQ-013018','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','Its values are given in','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fb30f9fdb27d21defc9cabb2197c44bf499bdc8c94269ceebc4d6291d805d2b8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13019','GHBC-REQ-013019','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','COEFFICIENT The site-dependant normalized elastic spectra for the three soil profiles are shown in Fig 5.10.5.3, their ordinates being defined as the smallest from the following expressions: R as = 1 + (α – 1).','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','b9f6892a12982e4d972c85253b68b81ab9e8655487c97515479ef18044da6b6e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-13020','GHBC-REQ-013020','GS 1207:2018',17,NULL,'17.10.5.3.2','GHBC-C-003639','T/T1 R as = α for soil types S1, S2, S3 = 0.8α for soil S3 if A, as defined in Clause 5.10.5.3.4, is greater than 0.3g R as = S. α.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":1,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"T/T1 R as = α for soil types S1, S2, S3 = 0.8α for soil S3 if A,"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":2,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":" R as = α for soil types S1, S2, S3 = 0.8α for soil S3 if A, as "}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6b54f628b06eea5f8b88ed4b01ddaab31ae3e7ebe47be99689dcb0e99fa01754','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
