('rowid-18703','GHBC-REQ-018703','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.5','GHBC-C-004845','a) Employ cool daylight fluorescent tubes for supplementary artificial lighting. b) Distribute luminaries with a separation of 2 m to 3 m in each bay of 3 m to 4 m width. c) Provide more supplementary lights such as twin tube luminaries in work areas where daylight is expected to be poor for example in the rear region of a room having single window and in the central region of a room having windows on opposite walls.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":2,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"minaries with a separation of 2 m to 3 m in each bay of 3 m to "},{"parameter":"measurement","value":3,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"s with a separation of 2 m to 3 m in each bay of 3 m to 4 m wid"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":3,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":" of 2 m to 3 m in each bay of 3 m to 4 m width. c) Provide more"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":4,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":" to 3 m in each bay of 3 m to 4 m width. c) Provide more supple"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','71e4b007ed12663c87ddec544c7a95c0e20ff90bc9433a867a970f992d37d280','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18704','GHBC-REQ-018704','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.5','GHBC-C-004845','In the vicinity of windows only single tube luminaries should be provided.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f4d2433baa51f83f85aca4a23865aa120a0a21c5954814165c82d785cf874f00','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18705','GHBC-REQ-018705','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','Energy conservation in lighting is effected by reducing wastage and using energy effective lamps and luminaires without sacrificing lighting quality.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0c24144d238641acd52e6581f1fc99afbbfa62e0f67b6e051179af1912a90ce8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18706','GHBC-REQ-018706','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','Measures to be followed comprise utilization of daylight, energy effective artificial lighting design by providing required illumination where needed, turning off artificial lights when not needed, maintaining lighter finishes of','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3c0251ecc684607f04c785f2ba4fb5b03d1cd9894c0245ca1a8a5603c0ae5ddd','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18707','GHBC-REQ-018707','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','ceiling, walls and furnishings, and implementing periodic schedule for cleaning of luminaires and group replacement of lamps at suitable intervals.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6901d220943e4f0aeb4de3d59513d55d9ee699bce1d66c7ffbc48b0f150e54d0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18708','GHBC-REQ-018708','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','Choice of light sources with higher luminous efficacy and luminaires with appropriate light distribution is the most effective means of energy saving in lighting.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','898a45e6b4862df33e10147f92105ab43fd21cac683a705f2865475c7b603f6d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18709','GHBC-REQ-018709','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','However, choice of light sources also depends on the other lighting quality parameters like colour rendering index and colour temperature or appearance.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','7f0f603be4284d677dfa30a270be9b746900e67843390126d517b1fab47ef501','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18710','GHBC-REQ-018710','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','For example, high pressure sodium vapour lamps, which have very high luminous efficacy, are not suitable for commercial interiors because of poor colour rendering index and colour appearance, but are highly desirable in heavy industries.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','70b51537fac90e8dab204a7945acf1e2ed82e68c54ebed38a5c58bfc3f1cfd9a','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-18711','GHBC-REQ-018711','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','Also the choice of light sources depends on the mounting height in the interiors.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','5911e181a8da15492aa324a79a5282134ebaf501e96fd6c9cac309ab378a6675','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18712','GHBC-REQ-018712','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6','GHBC-C-004846','For example, fluorescent lamps are not preferred for mounting beyond 7 m height, when high pressure gas discharge lamps are preferred because of better optical control due to their compact size.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":7,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"preferred for mounting beyond 7 m height, when high pressure ga"}]','[]',0.93,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','9975dc1fa68667aa24c0269bc57624c346604e56aa204ab74bc45e9934aa3058','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18713','GHBC-REQ-018713','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.1','GHBC-C-004847','Efficient artificial light sources and luminaires Luminous efficacy of some of the lamps used in lighting of buildings are given in Table 6 along with average life in burning hours, Colour Rendering Index and Colour Temperature.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','339a2e0b638773525b652139ac028255df31fb3589770289c35912d4dd92f450','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18714','GHBC-REQ-018714','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.1','GHBC-C-004847','Following recommendations may be followed in the choice of light sources for different locations:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','9670a644d824623fff352618fbb2644b777f6f08cee57bf6d91928146b3336cf','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18715','GHBC-REQ-018715','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.1','GHBC-C-004847','a)  For supplementary artificial lighting of work area in office building care should be taken to use fluorescent lamps, which match with colour temperature of the daylight. b)  For residential buildings fluorescent lamps and/or CFLS of proper CRI and CCT are recommended to match with the colours and interior design of the room. c)  For commercial interiors, depending on the mounting heights and interior design, fluorescent lamps, CFLS and low wattage metal halilde lamps are recommended.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6b510ddbb828b225fcecdbcd8e5230608529db0cdc987573d8ad04984ac51882','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18716','GHBC-REQ-018716','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.1','GHBC-C-004847','For highlighting the displays in show windows, hotels, etc., low wattage tubular or dichroic reflector type halogen lamps can be used. d)  For industrial lighting, depending on the mounting height and colour consideration fluorescent lamps, high pressure mercury vapour lamps or high','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6a2fd7993f878a7c7db1716aad7b130dbfc63758328407c1d19c78bce1227913','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18717','GHBC-REQ-018717','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.1','GHBC-C-004847','pressure sodium vapour lamps are recommended.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2f1800e745f4667b4b59be13c919e0e0ae7da5944b2b2473ec48cdcec72ce644','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18718','GHBC-REQ-018718','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.2','GHBC-C-004848','possible to save 75 to 80 percent energy if GLS lamps are replaced with CFL and 65 to 70 percent if replaced with fluorescent lamps.','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":80,"unit":"percent","operator":null,"context":"possible to save 75 to 80 percent energy if GLS lamps are repla"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":70,"unit":"percent","operator":null,"context":"e replaced with CFL and 65 to 70 percent if replaced with fluorescent "}]','[]',0.65,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','86adfd09804666ef5025d0187ceccf2f0137107b4f9018f6b2697f261651314c','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18719','GHBC-REQ-018719','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.2','GHBC-C-004848','Similar energy effective solutions are to be chosen for every application area.','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','da9d2e3a11d965984b7610ac67e45399faef2c64915e373ea24e758f1ce0ff66','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-18720','GHBC-REQ-018720','GS 1207:2018',28,NULL,'28.5.4.6.2','GHBC-C-004848','Similarly with white fluorescent tubes recommended for corridors and staircases, the electrical consumption reduces to 1/4.5 of the energy consumption with incandescent lamps.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','0f4e17299a09d138990045d4e4fa4687d5014b6a65a5a8905c1c2b4d30997e79','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
