('rowid-20342','GHBC-REQ-020342','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.1','GHBC-C-005191','In the case of external environment particular care should be taken to avoid a nuisance in the ‗silent‘ hours, and local authorities have statutory powers to ensure that noise from plant is limited.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3016dfc37f54d1d46c0f5f1157c15d652dd869e0bec347095204ffb07a8424c9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20343','GHBC-REQ-020343','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.1','GHBC-C-005191','It is important that expert advice be sought in dealing with noise and vibration problems, as for obvious reasons, the most economical solutions should be used, without impairing the performance.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','b199f3204c333304b7c7909e6618a6d4e6c5d33d0c5b38a3b18089ecf8f223ea','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20344','GHBC-REQ-020344','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.1','GHBC-C-005193','Reduction of externally created noise is mainly dealt with by choice of building profile and window construction.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','53dca1af2e54fccefa5a8d2672fceae0e8138a6f43535093cce553d978523ee2','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20345','GHBC-REQ-020345','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.1','GHBC-C-005193','The air conditioning','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','dee9f0bad5c030534799cd2563108f1a8ffe4e86d0053ffe63c1ca3a0c18aac0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20346','GHBC-REQ-020346','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.1','GHBC-C-005193','designer should, however, ensure that noise does not enter via air inlets or exhausts; it may be reduced by suitable attenuators.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','de05536f7eafc47ded24464ef6e77c9fae214aa5c1252950c351b9d23cf84811','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20347','GHBC-REQ-020347','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.2','GHBC-C-005194','Noise produced by the components of air conditioning and ventilation plant installed within the building can escape via ventilation grilles or door openings and can cause nuisance to neighbours.','fire',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fdd762483120fb2a7da263f7e6099c088c4e43b7f21c8c89ffdac8ccd19809fe','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20348','GHBC-REQ-020348','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.2','GHBC-C-005194','Equipment mounted outside the building may well need to be selected or installed with the noise problem in mind.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6c2e60f3b4fd21fad19bc5ad6fb96f3bbbc8fe4d6adb5f0c4005ae91fd8efcd3','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20349','GHBC-REQ-020349','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.2','GHBC-C-005194','Another type of generated noise is created by the air-circulating system itself and its associated equipment.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d0b122204ce4694efdc11c7ea00fb63c3f59d703b56f6896b28bc3f6226a015d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20350','GHBC-REQ-020350','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.2','GHBC-C-005194','Fans are an obvious source, but noise can be produced by turbulence, which may cause vibration of the ducts and noise transmission by air diffusers.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','46fc9900da71f9c3b5f8ff96a72266d539372afc74c695671a09f0ec1ece1b59','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-20351','GHBC-REQ-020351','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.2','GHBC-C-005194','This problem can be avoided by careful selection of and installation equipment or by the noise absorbing devices.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','91e0b583d78d26c66efefbec251d66b18e2a0c2e2f0dee3bde3c945e6b074d99','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20352','GHBC-REQ-020352','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.3','GHBC-C-005195','Noise transmitted through the building structure is particularly acute in modern frame and reinforced concrete buildings.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','548bda7360e005fa599fbc65bf07cba0063cb87e5f9a3a508153b7a7936bec9b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20353','GHBC-REQ-020353','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.3','GHBC-C-005195','Such noise can be controlled by isolating the machines from the structures, and from pipe work connected to the building, by suitable mountings and pipe couplings.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','080c04a24e27d68716c8878d07642f671a735bb09dcfd84467507ca850823d02','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20354','GHBC-REQ-020354','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.3','GHBC-C-005195','Another problem is the transmission of sound from one room to another via air ducting, ventilated ceilings or other continuous air space.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0b4adf49c3bcd1267884a31566336a29f3f94e71423c6030784f2f0b8cc28a34','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20355','GHBC-REQ-020355','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.3','GHBC-C-005195','Such sound includes the noise from machines and equipment and also of conversation, transmission of which can be embarrassing as well as annoying.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a90c9f97cb18077525569cdaaf64d39111bf7d71585a307a0a18f7c69af1a18a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20356','GHBC-REQ-020356','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.3','GHBC-C-005195','Again, the problem can be tackled by careful design and the inclusion of sound absorbing devices in ducts.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2d3a07999fd1a2a004b029605b5b4de4a4a55f41b01c64da762c3c97152c0597','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20357','GHBC-REQ-020357','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.4','GHBC-C-005196','Such noise arises from the stopping and starting of equipment, and the opening and closing of valves and dampers.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','99272bf06b3ad6485a060849a220dc5b89da0cbb8fa12cb1cffbebf4ec1cc2ef','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20358','GHBC-REQ-020358','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.4','GHBC-C-005196','This may or may not cause problems in the air conditioned spaces, but it is often objectionable to plant operators and maintenance engineers.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','509b29d47d871c3a768fcf814aadae6a399f87568c14738874ed52fdd167bdec','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20359','GHBC-REQ-020359','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.2.4','GHBC-C-005196','This should be considered by the air conditioning designer.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2fc83717be997c1c48964f47fd0f283c6bd64367b7eed9028d92945b82c76958','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20360','GHBC-REQ-020360','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.3','GHBC-C-005197','conditioning system could be from the following:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','9da268e0c8ccb76ce4c0121cff5d6859707bc38c26c135cceb8fabdfb7b9cf9d','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-20361','GHBC-REQ-020361','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.3','GHBC-C-005197','a) chillers; b) pumps; c) pipe supports; d) ducts; e) external noise in filtration though openings; f) fans; g) air noise through ducts; and h) compressors.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','96b658dc17511af1011321de48225854d4a0d4cc18a3146c7ab416070e6c594e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20362','GHBC-REQ-020362','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.4','GHBC-C-005198','The approach must always be to reduce the source noise rather than controlling them in the path.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','09a09213468eace0692e234bd2510819cc1e5f1637d6c04eaa56295b5e98316f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20363','GHBC-REQ-020363','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.1','GHBC-C-005200','The following measures should be adopted:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','901e90b8472420220514c8a3db6fafb9f8128b35c46179c6230ee1ddb7509865','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20364','GHBC-REQ-020364','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.1','GHBC-C-005200','a) Selection of RAC which has the least noise at various fan speeds; b) Installation at a serviceable height; c) Installation preferably in a wall or on a rigid window; d) Provision of only necessary slope as specified by the manufacturer, to avoid any unusual noise from the compressor because of tilting; e) Installation preferably in the middle portion of the wall/window to avoid additional directivity (do not install at the end of a wall); f) Ensure all leaks are sealed properly; g) Avoid condenser facing any high noisy areas, such as road/factory to avoid any such noise predominantly entering into the room; h) Do not provide any props at the back side bottom of the air conditioner unless specified by the manufacturer; i) Preparation of opening to suit the chassis with wooden frame of adequate rigidity and thickness.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a5e8bc4e79dc9212695c957923a1d5a5fe2d5ccfb2bb5196c31256acebb97f3a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20365','GHBC-REQ-020365','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005201','inn','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a256f7073ddbb5550a76016235fdaf1ceb8a855d26dffeba3f06eddad40e7a30','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20366','GHBC-REQ-020366','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005201','The following measures should be adopted:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','802ce111cc144dfc2938d62f5e1272b26e50af14d8582be2fd941a5b707aa043','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20367','GHBC-REQ-020367','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005201','a) Install the evapourator only on a rigid wall/ceiling or on a pedestal. b) Avoid installation over wooden/gypsum board partition.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','238c891e5a156f1e8924e42cbc73ddd4515f9135f27aa71155a84b8a6091918d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20368','GHBC-REQ-020368','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005201','Should a need arise, anchor the evapourator rigidly by using mild steel framework from the roof to avoid vibration. c) Provide proper ‗u‘ trap in the condensate water line to ensure a good water seal, which will also avoid sound penetration into the room from outside. d) If the capillary is in the evapourator, ensure that flow noise is avoided. e) Ensure proper return air entry back to the coil, since blowers working at higher static pressure will create higher noise. f) Select the condensers with top/side discharge depending upon location to avoid nuisance to neighbours. g) Place condensers on rigid platform, properly supported, propped and fixed firmly. h) Ensure all screws, bolts and nuts are firmly tightened since stiffening is more advantageous in higher frequencies for vibration reduction.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1bd495533ce45a7bcd278ce92ad384b62d7ebcdd755601243520d05a5d773bba','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20369','GHBC-REQ-020369','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.3','GHBC-C-005202','and ceiling suspended) The following measures should be adopted:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2744bdb00e33cd456f4f76de27f79d6f5995f2877e879b90c6278e60c7f9f501','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20370','GHBC-REQ-020370','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.3','GHBC-C-005202','a) Select indoor machine for specific air quantity and static pressure. b) Suspend the indoor machine and ducts without touching the members of the false ceiling or partitions. c) Ensure that ducts/duct supports do not touch the evapourator.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','41c736e26f707edbbcff8609feb2fa7ab32b0280f2fb0445342cf3cae72007aa','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-20371','GHBC-REQ-020371','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.4','GHBC-C-005203','The following measures should be adopted/considered:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','aa7e2a29d2cab502c241362da931fc49fe282c8e38d18edcdecd5abd70004747','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20372','GHBC-REQ-020372','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.4','GHBC-C-005203','a) If possible and if pressures allow, expand the air to a plenum chamber (of 2.5 m/s for normal office), which is acoustically lined inside. b) Stiffening of the plenum body is very critical since it could create a drumming noise. c) Plenum chambers with sound absorbing material are frequently used as silencers in air conditioning and ventilating','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":2.5,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"e air to a plenum chamber (of 2.5 m/s for normal office), which i"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','44f75b85d72b54a7e60e5997b59e2ff35a33b0ec51f1ec601a662194c50067c8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20373','GHBC-REQ-020373','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.4','GHBC-C-005203','systems and in testing facilities to reduce flow velocity and turbulence.','inspection',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','077baa7f10bad09bc42d893ba346c05f6a63c26295e09e638e800f737594bc9e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20374','GHBC-REQ-020374','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.4','GHBC-C-005203','The attenuation of these devices may be due to both dissipative and reactive effects.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2aa91ea4337016746bc5a29494433bb3582a03fe2ead077b1d44f8713be2d78b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20375','GHBC-REQ-020375','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.1','GHBC-C-005205','There are three basic types of centrifugal fans, backward curved, forward curved, and radial.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','b2af772b7daa0b704842ed0d649962e86b4dce6bdd4b0e162f628af8b810c550','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20376','GHBC-REQ-020376','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.1','GHBC-C-005205','Noise from centrifugal fans is dominantly a superimposition of discrete tones at the varying frequencies and broadband aerodynamic noise.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3323b8d8f09921a94c5024484cc5554920141a095ba530a58cf1e4ebe5f907c8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20377','GHBC-REQ-020377','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Axial fans derive their name from the fact that the airflow is along the axis of the fan.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','615763e2f8490a02681b01746a1559d317538fd6abdd0635021803a037ddd531','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20378','GHBC-REQ-020378','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','To avoid a circular flow pattern and to increase performance, guide vanes are usually installed downstream of the rotor.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','9617eca1b4da4fa20286eaf20097b90f75c149469bec9a369f0c97c271c38978','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20379','GHBC-REQ-020379','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Axial fans with exit guide vanes are called vane axial and those without guide vanes are called tube axial.','fire',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6e683b1bdd740be4e3b8a768de93d2d556bc37ae39b496a8c35bef7e1121525b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20380','GHBC-REQ-020380','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Axial fans generally operate at higher pressures than centrifugal fans and are usually considered noisier.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','ee4cb6eaf6f4ae74b892380d9636202e30e9ab4680d8fb311c2de0f7aff47fdb','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-20381','GHBC-REQ-020381','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Common applications include heating and ventilation systems.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a2d4da364ce311d2a8a34c5057c26e5564b53642913612217c8814efff0ee05f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20382','GHBC-REQ-020382','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Because of the large number of blades and high rotational speeds, noise from axial fans is generally characterized by strong discrete blade passing tones.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8e6d67dc7417067cff81559c793f2776ef410f5f456bb961a94f47d1e2fa513b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20383','GHBC-REQ-020383','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Variable inlet vane system may generate significantly low frequency noise as the vanes shut down.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2ca83d916d539a4f2ed0b6d718f22771340451c1a0de0b84dc466dd0190c0a31','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20384','GHBC-REQ-020384','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Additional attenuation with a corresponding additional pressure drop is required to attenuate the noise generated by the inlet vanes.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','76b18e3832bd82938e896ea1b0bcfb2a52ca321f36b90572716d4c28918b8218','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20385','GHBC-REQ-020385','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','Variable speed motors and drives and variable pitch fan blade systems are actually quieter at reduced air output than at full output.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8c8aa18ab8681299b64694d32e737f8446eb931db83390202e877d2774c29e99','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20386','GHBC-REQ-020386','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.2','GHBC-C-005206','The designer has the option of designing for maximum output as if the system were constant volume, or selecting the sound attenuation for a more normal operating point and allowing fan noise to exceed the design criteria on the rare occasions when the fan operates at full output.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','e58969009f3f8460a28bdaf1a590f42f390d01bc88abc9040146820af2fcdcb9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20387','GHBC-REQ-020387','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.3','GHBC-C-005207','To reduce fan noise, the following should be adopted:','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f55391b6cf4788e89bd1273c19ddfd72cae424e60913bb053974fa6350128886','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20388','GHBC-REQ-020388','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.3','GHBC-C-005207','a) Design the air distribution system for minimum resistance, since the','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','e0c8491f96395943d663a758b1c9b3ee3997ead6d1905ece19e019e6a56350d8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20389','GHBC-REQ-020389','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.3','GHBC-C-005207','sound generated by a fan, regardless of type, increases by the square of the static pressure.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','cc3d19307500859a1e581bf18f680db74881535390daad293e0a8d04d28ac827','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-20390','GHBC-REQ-020390','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.2.4.5.5.3','GHBC-C-005207','Turbulence can increase the flow noise generated by duct fittings and dampers in the air distribution systems especially at low frequencies. b) Examine the specific sound power levels of the fan designs for any given job.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a923ca6df2e706279783b193b3031425552ddc825b504ede7bc0e9559ac5f1c7','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
