('rowid-21582','GHBC-REQ-021582','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','2 When the daily noise exposure is composed of two or more periods of different Levels, their combined effect should be considered rather than the individual effect of each.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','341bffeedb9d74880e09dd20db50a3677d843c80e53f875fde12730e4dc61978','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21583','GHBC-REQ-021583','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','The combined levels may not exceed a daily noise dose, D of unity Where D is computed from the formula:','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','9032efc39a1999bf33f143e8a6666da172e73fd45b7484439db9470d5af3bc4b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21584','GHBC-REQ-021584','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','C C C    n 2 D1 .......','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','b259b97e79e7d692db009ff0e2c747fb2f3c6213d18f346a628b56eea2711bc7','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21585','GHBC-REQ-021585','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','T T T n 2 1','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','8cbf8d13153e988257a98792935cd74abfbf4bbf6faaad6efdab53a4b767cc7b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21586','GHBC-REQ-021586','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','Where, C1, C2 …… Cn indicate the total duration of exposure (in hours) at a given steady-state noise level; and T1, T2, …..','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','c08cd562aa3d9c8de46b2a976b3a241a2b825f106908c1b90dce116a8ece76ca','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21587','GHBC-REQ-021587','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','Tn are the noise exposure limits (in hours) for the respective levels given in the table or','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','0ca262a7bbc47724b0366ca2e558fe8479dfe522fd17162eacb32138b4283539','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21588','GHBC-REQ-021588','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','computed by the equation in Note 1.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','b9e0986514e0e28a6eea5e1c1b4076b268fee8ba72f6677a1c48ca73e35a8956','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21589','GHBC-REQ-021589','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.2','GHBC-C-005534','Exposure to continuous noise shall not exceed 115 dB(A) regardless of any value computed by the formula for the daily noise dose, D or by the equation given in Note 2.','prohibited',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.62,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','64b5e6a6579146a84ad99e496a13502e1526f3096e5c6e4279fb479311f59fe3','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21590','GHBC-REQ-021590','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.3','GHBC-C-005535','surfacing may be reduced by reducing the radiating area.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','69e46dacca340538ff0c81de45a2adfd77b206f8edb079747aa42650e16eba44','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21591','GHBC-REQ-021591','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.3','GHBC-C-005535','For example, if the area is halved, the noise intensity will be reduced by 3 dB and at low frequencies the reduction will be much greater.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','47f2a3af7c09c789bbbb564831f7c3e5039ffb72e64fda820ad453c55be98f4e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21592','GHBC-REQ-021592','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','machines and other equipment should be frames rather than cabinets or sheeted enclosures.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','67f8bb0481062a352f5d40add50c3e8662c426a48cb39f4ee1314f885b9e55f0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21593','GHBC-REQ-021593','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','If an enclosure is used, precaution should be taken to isolate it and line it on the inside with sound-absorbent material.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','775954029870ef1958413e229a790b47de2a42c71b72f9eb861dce47da9e7fb1','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21594','GHBC-REQ-021594','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The noise radiated by machinery guards can be minimized by making them of perforated sheet or of wire mesh.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','72897e762c3e14b7db7aa45a72526f59864e1496d7b5e9958fb707ebffcee7c5','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21595','GHBC-REQ-021595','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','29.4.9.4.3.5 Reducing transmission of mechanical vibration A vibrating source does not usually contain a large radiating surface but the vibration is conducted along mechanically rigid paths to surfaces that can act as effective radiator.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','49c7e193b5e51a8b7163333a87c76e20119142e057697eeb47ad413c6a0b4c8f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21596','GHBC-REQ-021596','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','If the rigid connecting paths are interrupted by resilient materials, the transmission of vibration and consequently the noise radiated may be greatly reduced.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','7728a945b9435841d6051c3cd44ae2cfb92474921562c3e4879c4420b2c64064','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21597','GHBC-REQ-021597','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The reduction depends on the ratio of the driving (forcing) frequency of the source to the natural frequency may be determined form static deflection under actual load as given in Fig. 1.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1c9c0dff9ee24b03dacd120b9032ee50562fe92561671e961d527cf41704d8c6','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21598','GHBC-REQ-021598','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Higher the ratio between the two frequencies, lesser is the transmissibility, which is defined as the ratio of the force transmitted through the resilient isolator to the exciting force applied to it.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ced41a76b390220883b7a5231bd6baf81cc7446071d59742a108f61b73bb774b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21599','GHBC-REQ-021599','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Transmissibility and the equivalent noise reduction for various frequency ratios are given in Fig.2.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','7f1b11e5e90c6dc53e279b49ca5658d785d325b107232474aab0d469559a4ece','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21600','GHBC-REQ-021600','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','For satisfactory operation, a ratio of 3:1 or more between the driving and natural frequencies is recommended.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ba98a846e70ead2c6baab177a62a10b67dc64ca5e32cd2bcbd68e287eab24835','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21601','GHBC-REQ-021601','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Materials for isolators and their position are given below:','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a26bb53223eb9f11ba6085771a449410b0167524cc3f38b4ec103b9f2c2c33b8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21602','GHBC-REQ-021602','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','a) Material for Isolators – Vibration isolators are usually made of resilient materials like steel in the form of springs, rubber cork and felt.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','63c0cc5413f466a967776582fef19a089aa80b0afacf39485b14ee57db64a2b7','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21603','GHBC-REQ-021603','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','1) Because of the large range of deflections obtainable in coil springs, they may isolate vibrations over a large spectrum of low frequencies.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','da631a0f47a4aa6df38471636cca1fd34c088a090761359a8cab02a30ff50648','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21604','GHBC-REQ-021604','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Metal springs transmit high frequency (from about two hundred to several thousand c/s) very readily.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','28f577161336f97ffa2758c7603e76ac7fff5ccace477bfdd31601b1f70c736b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21605','GHBC-REQ-021605','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Transmission of these frequencies can be reduced by eliminating direct contact between the spring and the supporting structure.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','c9de474cb35c3a5eb85957489ec2fc431086f0d5b9a60b0e22de41ce6c879ce8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21606','GHBC-REQ-021606','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Rubber or felt pads may be inserted between the ends of the spring and the surfaces to which it is fastened.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d809552884cfdf9bfdd56bbd931a2b3377683a6980ba62544afb107f77239896','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21607','GHBC-REQ-021607','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','2) Rubber in the form of pads may be used to isolate very effectively engines, motors, etc. It may be used in compression or in shear.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2cdd75364beb139a6a2f8921d08e942807cb8f002eef1b598b325224c1587d97','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21608','GHBC-REQ-021608','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Some rubber mountings use rubber-in-shear as the primary elastic elements and rubber-incompression as a secondary element which furnishes snubbing action if the mounting is subjected to an overload.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','382af0be24cbaf22fbb1803cc5021fed414deb58741ddb650ca92cd27f0a1b0d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21609','GHBC-REQ-021609','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','3) Felt or cork or both may be used as resilient mats or pads under machine bases.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3bdd64bcc1f82aab59a12d3f1b59c0cc822afda192b46b13dbc6285e84724fd7','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21610','GHBC-REQ-021610','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The load per unit area shall be chosen to produce enough deflection for the isolation required; and shall be such that at this deflection, it is not loaded beyond its elastic limit.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','5f6ae6c4ca6ddec84201fac280d43a9fe81ddc2205e86779496d475ec87a775a','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21611','GHBC-REQ-021611','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','b) Position of Isolator – The normal position of the isolators is between the machine and its foundation.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','bd8d82b930fe39280a8739d4b52f315a5128e6eac935d5af5f271c56ab173e7f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21612','GHBC-REQ-021612','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','However, if the forcing frequency of the machine is low (less than 10 H2) and vibration isolators with the requisite deflection for this location are not available, the machine','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"comparison","value":10,"unit":null,"operator":"less than","context":"quency of the machine is low (less than 10 H2) and vibration isolators w"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":10,"unit":"h","operator":null,"context":"the machine is low (less than 10 H2) and vibration isolators wit"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a4b448e8a4cdfcfa546b190e5610443e2a3324983761945b1c873177b8d0afef','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21613','GHBC-REQ-021613','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','may be bolted directly to an independent heavy inertia concrete base and the available','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','b8b898942a2e94eb18f0beec3d3d5541c806a277f124cc87b9bf6f338f407ad8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21614','GHBC-REQ-021614','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','vibration isolators used below the concrete base.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f8986b821cdb548f79be54ef74db3091a2f71e4e567bd12f3a4e4c0987f7c2cc','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21615','GHBC-REQ-021615','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','1) Large press and drop hammers which create serious impact vibration in heavy machine shops may be mounted rigidly on very massive blocks of concrete having weights several times greater than the weights of the supported machines.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ce0da585c7396cd9f067cdd00035d015be6a503ac2f8234ad1674277ae924396','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21616','GHBC-REQ-021616','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The inertia blocks may, in turn, be isolated from the building structure by large wooden blocks and with thick pads of cork.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','5eeee9d0973cb27c52c1fac8d8179169e555b7d427f3cb66cc00b9905e66a5b2','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21617','GHBC-REQ-021617','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','2) In critical installations (see Note), attempt should be made to locate the resilient mounts in a plane which contains the centre of gravity of the mounted assembly.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','c4c83c50fc92b69098226c61c9ddf275cd17ac2c6f7e90ac060981b1ea0d4868','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21618','GHBC-REQ-021618','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','It is also preferable to locate the mounts laterally as far away as possible from the centre of the machine.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f3bebf0103d1a636f0005b483a72b03e5b841f61d2c6f36b84dbb3299d76a728','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21619','GHBC-REQ-021619','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Note: Critical installations are those installations where transmission of vibration from these installations will seriously hamper the normal working.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1e0da7b9844e3ca8d926209a227b8ae3cadbb97e6a0eaa5a5543694d1fa12034','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21620','GHBC-REQ-021620','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','3) Rigid mechanical ties between vibrating machine and building structure, short-circuit or reduce the effectiveness of isolators.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','54e60d9ac2f47b4797d6911640f85a5cff41f3ad4db3a8e81fc4f46c9f6b8fdb','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21621','GHBC-REQ-021621','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Loose and flexible connections should be inserted in all pipes and conduits leaving from the vibrating machine.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d4e6b1cce5be2432adb1460f02e346a0f02b9e3579b0d4c44a6332d0de8d9080','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21622','GHBC-REQ-021622','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Where flexible connections are impracticable, bends should be inserted into the pipes or the pipes themselves should be supported on vibration mounts for a considerable distance from the source.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','808fbb0ef94d12288557c1750181e6875560a3dca332af4dccec2c34dd9675dd','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21623','GHBC-REQ-021623','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','4) Flexibility of foundation – The effect of flexibility of the foundation on the isolator transmissibility shall be considered in the selection of practical vibration isolating mountings.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','01155c80ef3f84856afe555ede0d296ec50b0cec5a86f7dea7345904e0dff90d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21624','GHBC-REQ-021624','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The simplified vibration isolation theory assumes a completely rigid foundation.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','57ef9e47666488955b2530e1054844b850e50320fd096d11f58c5ab7b6bb4419','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21625','GHBC-REQ-021625','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','However, in practice, this can never be achieved.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','719058f296833f7d0edb6c2e25be5af4c709d275fcb7253c5480057ec850223e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21626','GHBC-REQ-021626','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','The foundation is never actually completely rigid.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','979850d97f29015aac6cd07ec9c8ec252536c0e7ce6ff2c7430888daa979f72d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21627','GHBC-REQ-021627','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Generally, the relatively low stiffness of the isolation system permits the assumption of the foundation to be rigid.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','e9afc30a97630ca6da8205a07d170faf00b70d77d296e1c64f05f5654938722f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21628','GHBC-REQ-021628','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','However, if the stiffness of the isolator is allowed to become comparable to the foundation stiffness (or greater), the deflection of the isolator will become smaller and the foundation will also deflect with increased transmissibility and','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','4ec2dd61b350e046cec42227188837819b9d2513c293bbc01109b0eb25e5e974','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21629','GHBC-REQ-021629','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','decreased isolator efficiency.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a9ac61115e8114f1f8931e457cbb89dab5d0841a8fce5d1f92786ebee007cfcd','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21630','GHBC-REQ-021630','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','In a dynamic sense, supporting foundation or floors should have natural frequency as high and be as stiff as possible compared to the system being isolated.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','99d6af855e2aa61dc75c4f4c1fd25103f91335e70d8641592617c457f39a53ba','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21631','GHBC-REQ-021631','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','Good design practice requires that the isolators should be designed assuming a rigid foundation with the stipulation that the selected machine isolation system frequency should be well below the foundation frequency.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d76ea4d2534db02a4a64058e7bf52cb24db88eead7ed1a3f79d25e04fde7839d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21632','GHBC-REQ-021632','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.3.4','GHBC-C-005536','This point should specially be kept in mind when installing machines at upper levels in buildings because supported slabs generally have lower natural frequencies (low stiffness) than slabs on grade in basement or ground floor locations.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ec6953400488251be6e408a36ea409f00c0a555f8e303975122a6bee686ccfe8','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21633','GHBC-REQ-021633','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4','GHBC-C-005537','and barriers (Noise Control)','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8abb7711f40ce088254588c8c477a53b9e5e6ab27007565864ef3b765c083beb','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21634','GHBC-REQ-021634','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','Air borne noise generated by a machine may be reduced by placing the machine in an enclosure or behind a barrier.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','66c4434f170151611b8e2f793144868640127f693edd566eb9ab3b5ed04231bc','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21635','GHBC-REQ-021635','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','The enclosure may be in the form of close fitting acoustic box around the machine such that the operator performs his normal work outside the box and thus is not subjected to the high noise levels of the machine.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8e10fd00114f47f0af4a078b0bc85f1ada81c22615e82a961642223b541740aa','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21636','GHBC-REQ-021636','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','The enclosure may be made of sheet metal lined inside with an acoustical material.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0583943c3fa446d7a69a810635a09abb57f0712327a273e6116afa1fb052c720','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21637','GHBC-REQ-021637','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','Where size of the machine, working area and the operation do not permit close-fitting enclosures, the machine may be housed in a room of its own.','approval',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','4089f617f0c3b28cd3582798f6d29e00af66f52d9e9d30530e18d11d56aa68a1','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21638','GHBC-REQ-021638','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','The inside of the enclosure should be lined with sound-absorbing materials to reduce the noise level of the contained sound.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','9416e2aa3ade94a0732097fb9d884a5e1986679d3c23877d6eced416afb5feca','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21639','GHBC-REQ-021639','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.1','GHBC-C-005538','The bounding walls of the enclosures shall also have adequate transmission loss to provide desired insertion loss.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8f4a6f98cf619cc7784c5317df1c6b98824c84478a26e37f7b6fcd2b20fb2594','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21640','GHBC-REQ-021640','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.2','GHBC-C-005539','A partial reduction of noise in certain directions may be obtained by ‗barriers‘ or partial enclosures or partial height walls.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','522c6540b97b5373ccbe81c626beaa52db1cd6853a387aab20a9e3c6a508982f','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21641','GHBC-REQ-021641','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.2','GHBC-C-005539','Two-sided or three-sided barrier, with or without a top and','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','26c909c54c332e8a937c30c724bafbedf4cbb9dd806362d63896eff7042f9e20','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21642','GHBC-REQ-021642','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.2','GHBC-C-005539','invariably covered on the machine side with acoustic absorption material should face a wall covered with sound-absorbing material.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','81826589090387bda0dc5ae14f2817adfd2aaafd8471738d93ae88dac83155fa','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21643','GHBC-REQ-021643','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.4.2','GHBC-C-005539','If the top of the enclosures is open, the reduction may be increased by placing sound-absorbing material on the ceiling overhead.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d056694f461e0b80dc276d2e9c578971f04502ba79b5e9dafdc3cf755c6ab544','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21644','GHBC-REQ-021644','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.1','GHBC-C-005541','and side walls In order to reduce the general reverberant noise level in machine shops, acoustical material be placed on the ceiling and side walls.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','c93e7cbedf5e74f3435d0eb3fea25d5803118fac03aa3e6917f650609236e5fd','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21645','GHBC-REQ-021645','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.1','GHBC-C-005541','With this treatment 3 to 6 dB reduction of middle and high frequency noise may be achieved.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','4d8606fcbec2534d45dafef49e964d9f0c04563ccc54f2f49fac7a6afaf8097f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21646','GHBC-REQ-021646','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.1','GHBC-C-005541','While the noise level at the source, affecting the operator, may not be reduced materially, the treatment would bring down the general noise level away from the source in reverberant field.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3c97041e8fefcf6adeaa1af2ef26d3f878c0ea5957a56860e1a619b54fee5980','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21647','GHBC-REQ-021647','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005542','For efficient noise reduction ‗functional sound absorbers‘ may be clustered as near the machines as possible.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fb422a8abeeedb5f53a4c98bcc94a4ab06425c8d9ae9e6ce2e5509055fdb6c33','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21648','GHBC-REQ-021648','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005542','These units may be suspended and distributed in any pattern to obtain lower noise levels within the machine shop.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a5cc646ee39164e1ebc7c0e238c78936c03ecb4fa746a1f3948b0c04ed26e7af','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21649','GHBC-REQ-021649','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005542','Compared on the basis of equal total exposed surface areas, functional sound absorbers have higher noise reduction coefficients (NRC) than conventional acoustical materials placed directly on ceilings and walls.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d511892e61226c328b5254d178a66ba957999e6f18c8587657eb93000943584a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21650','GHBC-REQ-021650','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.9.4.5.2','GHBC-C-005542','29.4.10 LABORATORIES AND TEST HOUSES','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":4.1,"unit":"l","operator":null,"context":"29.4.10 LABORATORIES AND TEST HOUSES"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','77af39a312fd2b11d144224258aafcb2235fa6f56d3009044ab025d1ab53f770','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21651','GHBC-REQ-021651','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.1.1','GHBC-C-005544','In a test house or laboratory, where research workers and scientists are engaged in performing sophisticated experiments, the external noise is mostly contributed by noise emitting buildings (workshops, machine rooms), airports, railway stations and general traffic noises.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','81e757530766cf094885b72a85335e22eeedc68bfc0e97d8ab0faebc1009c784','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21652','GHBC-REQ-021652','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.1.1','GHBC-C-005544','The outdoor sources of noise in a college laboratory include noises produced in  a playground as well.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0106408f6a5884896b1fbcbbdbfc0cc6cbea3a9a14d4f886ace244ce4a53c1e0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21653','GHBC-REQ-021653','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.1.2','GHBC-C-005545','The following sources mainly contribute to indoor noises in research institutions/college laboratories. a) workshops, machine rooms, cafeteria, etc.;','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0173e3423543440b5ec2d6f6eaadd0fc3aa5c2ea880f4444ca8e57adc554f0da','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21654','GHBC-REQ-021654','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.1.2','GHBC-C-005545','b) air-conditioning and exhaust fans; c) noise-produced within the test house or laboratory while performing experiments; and d) typing or other machine noises, telephone service, lift, sanitary services, etc.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','b1efd4d75e4ae2e1e6a8935882ada0b1a9ae3057322cc6c0f6151d7158b6d9f0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21655','GHBC-REQ-021655','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.1','GHBC-C-005547','While planning for a laboratory or test house, care should be taken in the design that n noise emitting installations should exist in its neighbourhood.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f7cd13d209775d9df95e9f36b12709756855e5ee97699e3ca23b39d5b9d49697','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21656','GHBC-REQ-021656','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.1','GHBC-C-005547','However, where outdoor noises exist, such as from local factory, heavy traffic airports, railway lines, sport grounds or busy markets, buildings should be kept as far away as possible from the source of noise.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f5de93ba3be4e25b31cec23a2e7b46ba478092213c2a324f46c2882fee975da5','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21657','GHBC-REQ-021657','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.1.1','GHBC-C-005548','towards the noise sources should be minimal.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','866f7ee1c4c8776c83bebfd88a82261a630ccb7d6666fa071c537f89b65b6d3f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21658','GHBC-REQ-021658','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.1.1','GHBC-C-005548','Minimum amount of glazing should be placed on walls directly facing the noise sources.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0b5ecd3e7cc02b13c02f6ab6d5d9819fc245fdee8c4cf6da91e8b11a68fe95f9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21659','GHBC-REQ-021659','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.1','GHBC-C-005550','separate from the quiet ones.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','ed0e42d6a7370d8c0d989236e7e25106f71af8241f87238b2958603736f94364','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21660','GHBC-REQ-021660','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.1','GHBC-C-005550','The location of laboratories or test houses should be so chosen that it is cut off from the noisy zones.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1a8c49d30b728919bb77d1c0d3b6ada8d3909198954a0d1757af17b3143c8ed1','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21661','GHBC-REQ-021661','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.1','GHBC-C-005550','Where there are offices attached to a laboratory, provision should be made to treat the offices and to use acoustical partitions, to achieve a sound isolation Dw at least 35 dB.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"comparison","value":35,"unit":null,"operator":"at least","context":" achieve a sound isolation Dw at least 35 dB."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a06b9b6d0ba91cb78c5660a740611e92343f3296a4665adbae249e4eb6221ea1','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21662','GHBC-REQ-021662','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.2','GHBC-C-005551','reflecting surfaces and bare furnishings are found, which produce very reverberant conditions.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8f84ea7815974cc3eb772b15f36aaa2ffdbf545078dcd21b5772e4fc33b5ee8b','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21663','GHBC-REQ-021663','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.2','GHBC-C-005551','The noise condition still deteriorates when noise producing instruments are switched on or a heavy object is dropped on the floor.','electrical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2ae706f117ee45e49953e37b67979bfabca2d88c4dc583068ae52bdbcc4f114f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21664','GHBC-REQ-021664','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.2','GHBC-C-005551','Under these conditions, sound absorbing treatment of the space is very essential.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','60177f9b8c2381f2f342ea1d780efccf098e512ff1c836b1ffcbfd0020945692','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21665','GHBC-REQ-021665','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.2','GHBC-C-005551','Sound absorbing ceilings are recommended to deaden such noises.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','00949c383425d87604b83bfd6ed2c3840449ee3597b29b2518ffa2e08ce43a5c','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21666','GHBC-REQ-021666','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.2','GHBC-C-005551','Rubber buffers may also be fitted to the legs of furniture.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0dd7c5b949983882efe10e227320bf3157ed32f33d4d15f48ff6fa22a179c881','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21667','GHBC-REQ-021667','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.3','GHBC-C-005552','houses where scientists and researchers are engaged in work and/or simultaneously busy in calculations or desk work requiring high degree of mental concentration, use of sound absorbing screens is recommended.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ed97a4f97875c973b48376faff207a3154d7d2b5a484122b9cfe208d717e130e','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21668','GHBC-REQ-021668','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.4','GHBC-C-005553','house or laboratory and corridors or general','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','92ca8b4b3ffd98f6554b759cad5cb8db4dba42e83ccaa2ef910bf86234550c47','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21669','GHBC-REQ-021669','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.4','GHBC-C-005553','circulation space should be well kept in mind and due care should be taken of the type of doors and the manner of their fittings etc. Transmission of noise through service ducts, pipes, lifts and staircases should also be guarded.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f858ef01365275bf4bf4780ca041410750e1de932f5549eaca247bd8ae0e150f','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21670','GHBC-REQ-021670','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.4','GHBC-C-005553','Telephones should preferably be placed in a separate small enclosure or acoustically efficient telephone booth.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','ffb4b0de4cc33399acb685ad6699db10fca640a883fa4f8048b59cdda441747c','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21671','GHBC-REQ-021671','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.5','GHBC-C-005554','house from structure borne noises originating from upper floor, sandwich type floor construction is recommended.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8318a2ecbcc92ce9be25612b756643331b6f0e17849503c62085ff78a7a91a69','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21672','GHBC-REQ-021672','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.6','GHBC-C-005555','the provision of double glazed windows is necessary to reduce the heat losses, care should be taken to provide sealed double windows rather than double glazing in a single window.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','57c5efc0e2371c8cca6145c56d1e24ab29fc29b4f4aa1bafac31cdca623be462','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21673','GHBC-REQ-021673','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.10.2.2.6','GHBC-C-005555','Note – Double glazed windows for sound isolation should have a minimum gap of 100 mm between the two glasses.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":100,"unit":"mm","operator":null,"context":" should have a minimum gap of 100 mm between the two glasses."}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fcd060826f64715f9d780e04c19c50462cb3d6f7e1885f9a79df5575bd7751e6','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21674','GHBC-REQ-021674','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1','GHBC-C-005557','It is important that law courts and council chambers be protected from the intrusion of outdoor noise and from indoor noise arising both from ancillary offices and circulation spaces.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f90cdabd41c12854cf7518938d137ec4beadd3b70b51ba016b8dafe24fd31fe9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21675','GHBC-REQ-021675','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1','GHBC-C-005557','The general recommendations on site planning given in Part 3 apply to law courts and municipal buildings, but in the larger buildings at least, further protection against outdoor noise can be obtained by planning offices and other rooms around the court rooms or chambers, and separating the offices from the central rooms by means of corridors.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3338d2f3a39db65dc0d3185cdd2f2120735e7104ce1e7c7714982c426b76a758','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21676','GHBC-REQ-021676','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1','GHBC-C-005557','This arrangement is usually convenient to the function of the buildings.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0bfb4e38c9531d7f3e7e3b4aa7ed7d929736863b96e1373ec081c65666d3b8c0','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21677','GHBC-REQ-021677','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.1','GHBC-C-005558','and the central rooms should have a sound reduction index, Rw, of not less than 50 dB (for example 230 mm brick) to insulate against airborne noise in the corridors.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"comparison","value":50,"unit":null,"operator":"not less than","context":"sound reduction index, Rw, of not less than 50 dB (for example 230 mm brick)"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":230,"unit":"mm","operator":null,"context":" less than 50 dB (for example 230 mm brick) to insulate against ai"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d888ed8474a32c532f5215024cb122ba680983865988ec8d9ac05dca07144738','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21678','GHBC-REQ-021678','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.1','GHBC-C-005558','Entrances from halls or corridors into court rooms or counsel chambers should be through baffle lobbies with two sets of quiet action doors.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','028e3e9fa4ec32c734c85d96f142940ab6f15e3d9081bc8cd5e9c492391e2ebc','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21679','GHBC-REQ-021679','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.1','GHBC-C-005558','Sound absorbing treatment on ceilings and upper parts or walls or entrance lobbies is recommended.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8d2304d44e47826f05cf884073fac36842350e0ddeeb264cfeec6f370aab6b0a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21680','GHBC-REQ-021680','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','room or chamber including steps and seating areas set aside for the public should have a resilient floor finish to reduce the noise of','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','85602d5d3cf481e28bca040512be627df470ca464594d8034dcd63cc6416f6b6','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21681','GHBC-REQ-021681','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','footsteps and shuffling of feet.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a0683c5b86daa81f7c6a13d75c0a7e94e00eee99496afd6260959b576f51e17a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21682','GHBC-REQ-021682','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','Any tip-up seats should be quiet in action.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','e76b6332fcaf0daeae838a1150a212eae126a0527707b0eba4e61e6765a9f7c1','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21683','GHBC-REQ-021683','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','29.4.11.1.3 Sound absorbing treatment applied for acoustic purposes serves also to reduce the build-up of noise within the room and, part of the treatment should be applied in a band to the perimeter of the ceiling to absorb intruding outdoor noise.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":1.3,"unit":"s","operator":null,"context":"29.4.11.1.3 Sound absorbing treatment appli"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f9d41a5aa1e5165946a9e6a7b93cf27bc39902428aed465889fdfbe236f70bcb','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21684','GHBC-REQ-021684','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','It is often desirable to keep the centre part of the ceiling free of absorbent material for acoustic reasons.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1c3c123bce263d0b1abd9adcbb347553d7194c782346a25d027cf8013b2e1953','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21685','GHBC-REQ-021685','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','29.4.11.2 Libraries, museums and art galleries Quiet conditions for reading and study are essential in these types of buildings and, since their occupancy is not noise producing, intruding noise is more noticeable and distracting.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":11.2,"unit":"l","operator":null,"context":"29.4.11.2 Libraries, museums and art gall"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','d6dbe23f0553ec8d6e6b49dd99b959f63194cc41ae89fc73ea9abe431f8fa9a9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21686','GHBC-REQ-021686','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','Every opportunity therefore should be taken to plan for noise defence, both in respect of siting of the building and internal planning.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fd91cc6fd09b861b5aaebe6f67eca754fff91552966e21d14662d0f853f1f45d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21687','GHBC-REQ-021687','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','When possible, stack rooms, store rooms and administrative offices should be planned to screen reading rooms, print rooms and lecture rooms from noise sources.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','94106272c84c66c2a3e43b8f8dceaf0b2ace557a90d0e09f13ee0fc1abcab911','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21688','GHBC-REQ-021688','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.1.2','GHBC-C-005559','In public libraries, the reference library and lecture rooms should receive first consideration; the lending library, newspaper and periodical rooms have a higher background noise and are secondary in importance.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2c3d945dce55075d889e4c207129c7f2e5678f8332f4909c153002d1b9d12d12','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21689','GHBC-REQ-021689','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.1','GHBC-C-005560','galleries echoes from lofty, large doomed or concave ceilings are often a nuisance.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','1a4106a31900e2c7331eceeff8e92236817bafe02c4add7a3da477f7fb019a81','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21690','GHBC-REQ-021690','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.1','GHBC-C-005560','Small noises such as footsteps, coughs, chair scraping and closing of books are reinforced by reverberation, and concave surfaces even when treated with a sound absorbent may focus these noises.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6d42e3571565b75d2b212e8d10917db98a39030c65f1798b50f1759093a38c6d','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21691','GHBC-REQ-021691','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.1','GHBC-C-005560','Treated flat ceilings, if not too high, obviate these troubles.','conditional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','3e6690035437c41dcd4338036e6e90e98b3fcfd701d7cfed22b0b8510f5ec749','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21692','GHBC-REQ-021692','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.1','GHBC-C-005560','Books on shelves in libraries constitute a valuable wall absorbent.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','434970b37a09c435d3740326edaf34193889783a79f20fe2ea4a378fa3afccea','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21693','GHBC-REQ-021693','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.2','GHBC-C-005561','Floor finishes are important.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0fc76cc505d3d7c6c3ca5187ec862ed9cd08b9e2107b880a99b775c0dcb01d78','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21694','GHBC-REQ-021694','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.2','GHBC-C-005561','The impact noise of footsteps on marble, terrazzo or wood block flooring, and especially on hardwood strip and battern flooring, can be disturbing both within the room in which the noise is generated and the rooms below.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f32d0089dd9ab14b1ffb0981f23b4a823a7d6f7571f8b077d48d01439e635ff6','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21695','GHBC-REQ-021695','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.2','GHBC-C-005561','On solid floors, resilient floor finishes, such as rubber, cork and linoleum on an underlay, are highly desirable.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','bfa021750ed8c8996c002b934be72b01700cdf90ee45b69827095cac96a72b51','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21696','GHBC-REQ-021696','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.2','GHBC-C-005561','In the children‘s clauses of libraries and museums they are essential.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6086b45e1c4d1baa5bd393327436215e6c93a0f1237b238a35fbaee667ad1ae6','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21697','GHBC-REQ-021697','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.2','GHBC-C-005561','In existing buildings, rubber linoleum or vinyl asbestos tiles laid over the floor in the traffic areas are often a solution to the problem.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','748c4574818b2182cbba4a1810d43a54711ea5a332521d8982f2a8ce562a5772','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21698','GHBC-REQ-021698','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.3','GHBC-C-005562','research establishments, office buildings and science buildings having machines and testing benches, should be planned in a quiet part of the building.','inspection',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','62e29c401ed68137824ba4ec9bb16e83eeb8ebb9a86049b965aa578096dcc166','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21699','GHBC-REQ-021699','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.3','GHBC-C-005562','Walls enclosing the library should normally have a sound reduction index, Rw of not less than 50 dB (for example 230mm brick) and baffle lobbies should be planned between the library and halls and corridors.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"comparison","value":50,"unit":null,"operator":"not less than","context":" sound reduction index, Rw of not less than 50 dB (for example 230mm brick) "},{"parameter":"measurement","value":230,"unit":"mm","operator":null,"context":" less than 50 dB (for example 230mm brick) and baffle lobbies sho"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','0a9e7adfa1d8a986fafb96d6184b348d858599de9f679ff1c5bc0bd09231be9d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21700','GHBC-REQ-021700','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.2.3','GHBC-C-005562','Wall fencing on to corridors or other noisy areas should not have fanlights unless they are double- glazed and non-operable.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','9ba2866e116ade00fdc58a634aa2c0ac07e7c846f0d578d96b2a3ba68eabecd5','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-21701','GHBC-REQ-021701','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3','GHBC-C-005563','The sources of noise that have to be considered in concert halls, opera house, theatres and similar auditorium buildings are as follows: a) Outdoor noise entering through walls, roofs, doors, windows or ventilation openings; b) Noise from any other hall in the same building, especially if let out separately for revenue; c) Noise from foyers, service rooms and other ancillary rooms, particularly rehearsal rooms; and d) Noise from air conditioning plant, etc. and the crosstransmission of other internal noises via ventilating duct system.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8e0552322f8d0818ed65205781ad4e082dfb90cdd697c96f405adee80a1c4c54','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21702','GHBC-REQ-021702','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.1','GHBC-C-005564','outdoor noise, all auditorium buildings now need more care in siting than formerly.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2b733db23c2846da6cff2fa1fe6d87e5f803a170eff761f8ddc29106b0ffc31c','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21703','GHBC-REQ-021703','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.1','GHBC-C-005564','For','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','86b471e75b33b4e3f51efeb9228cbeb67ceef6b0be5a1eb4d739ff3d2ef00000','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21704','GHBC-REQ-021704','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.1','GHBC-C-005564','auditoria (dB)','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8d03bc68bfdeafc00a2a27607c1301a12229fa000c563253bbe6b55642d886bf','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21705','GHBC-REQ-021705','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.3','GHBC-C-005565','reduction index, Rw, likely to be required for the envelope of an auditorium in a city to protect it against external noise is of the order of 65 dB for a concert hall or 55-60 dB for a theatre.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','02d97ccc432c903f0c4bf1297395fd0150c076af6b47b55ad4f6fcb929a1dd68','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21706','GHBC-REQ-021706','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.3','GHBC-C-005565','This reduction should be provided on','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6d747939c2e13c4ac61825a35ea37fe2ea3d95ec0f8b1c21277cb749f1d0af31','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21707','GHBC-REQ-021707','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.3','GHBC-C-005565','listening to speech or music, very low background noise level is desirable; in concert halls especially the quietest possible conditions should be provided because the pauses and moments of silence which are an essential element of music cannot otherwise be given full value.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2b157663bfc6632547eb7e08d0e501267d62c17259bd242c09d2f5fe19989dff','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21708','GHBC-REQ-021708','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.3','GHBC-C-005565','Therefore, sites at crossroads or close to steel railway bridges, religious places or near churches where bell ringing is practiced, should be avoided unless very high standards of structural sound insulation are contemplated.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','9137402cafde4a6c882544687d699c2874ac111645244f1c5148205fb47b6c36','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21709','GHBC-REQ-021709','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.3','GHBC-C-005565','Sites adjoining underground railways may also prove unsatisfactory at basement levels owing to low-pitched noise or rumble transmitted through the ground: special isolation measure need to be adopted for isolating large buildings from ground vibration of this sort.','environmental',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f9392981cd162681b9d28d5a12d99f5ef44020ae294654e04587b0cdb361096a','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21710','GHBC-REQ-021710','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,'29.4.11.3.2','GHBC-C-005566','halls and theatres on city sites a noise survey of the site should be made; a suitable sound reduction value for the structure of the building can then be chosen so as to keep down to certain maximum noise levels within the auditorium.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','2eb32c2866935af2e09f364ce7e253296191c9c0e485fa35f2bdc1b7840d3c9a','2026-08-15 13:56:13');
