('rowid-21882','GHBC-REQ-021882','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','F-3 AIR-BORNE SOUND INSULATION F-3.1 General The sound insulation of structural elements such as walls and floors always varies with frequency, the insulation rising in general as the frequency rises.','structural',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a1aab829349bfe4f20151f4350a4d4abbec1d0039656be6222aa34765063c928','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21883','GHBC-REQ-021883','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','F-3.2 Terminology Results from field measurements are usually expressed in terms of the weighted standardized level difference, while laboratory measurements are usually expressed in terms of the sound reduction index.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','8480aa41c27d2f1833282757a6dc36e82c0e26adb628b97524210bec8b1079d9','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21884','GHBC-REQ-021884','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','In the absence','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','c9991874d1f9aac3081a2bf0360ec00a7657b00b61b25ad27d68d8189c986964','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21885','GHBC-REQ-021885','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','of significant flanking transmission, the numerical difference between the weighted standardized level difference and the sound reduction index of a wall or floor is usually small for furnished rooms in dwellings, and so either quantity may be used in considering principles; for this purpose it is, therefore, convenient to use the general term insulation.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f39fa909c841bf3d4789b49b3feeba81cfb04612cfc48774f82c37d06835c549','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21886','GHBC-REQ-021886','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','F-3.3 Mass law An approximate empirical relationship has been established between sound insulation and mass for single leaf constructions as shown in Fig. 8.','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":-3.3,"unit":"m","operator":null,"context":"F-3.3 Mass law An approximate empiric"}]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ad964910dfd6d3ad849ca6bfad634a3d0093b5827312d77e62058eaf30d5889c','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21887','GHBC-REQ-021887','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','This so called ‗mass law‘ gives a useful first approximation to the behaviour of a single sheet or plate.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','7c525a3f476bb16505194c3c92ea60bfb473f648f4b3a1123668446f30fed32c','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21888','GHBC-REQ-021888','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','In','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','bdd1d14644d005ebee76f92fe95b4d2e8661cdd815cc423fce22305a59739ffb','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
('rowid-21889','GHBC-REQ-021889','GS 1207:2018',29,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-005572','practice, the sound insulation predicted by the mass law may not be attained because of factors such as the coincidence effect, which is outlined in F-3.4.','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','["is 10","is 10","IS 11050:1984"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a483ff2b480f83582a64f4b8560ec85da0c55e7d1581bd37fd686270399d0b0d','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
