('rowid-26323','GHBC-REQ-026323','GS 1207:2018',37,'37.9',NULL,'GHBC-C-007197','Installation of solar PV shall cover the following: • Private Office and Commercial/Industrial buildings throughout Ghana that are above 5,000 m2 total gross floor area; • Public buildings located in all the Regional and District Capitals that are above 500 m2 in total gross floor area; • Residential buildings throughout Ghana that are above 75 m2. •','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":5000,"unit":"m2","operator":null,"context":"roughout Ghana that are above 5,000 m2 total gross floor area; • Pub"},{"parameter":"measurement","value":500,"unit":"m2","operator":null,"context":"trict Capitals that are above 500 m2 in total gross floor area; • "},{"parameter":"measurement","value":75,"unit":"m2","operator":null,"context":"roughout Ghana that are above 75 m2. •"}]','[]',0.93,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','c02f48552b52fc33e72ec01fcb68c384bfa9f061708ee40bf3396eb8d84ea70b','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26324','GHBC-REQ-026324','GS 1207:2018',37,'37.10',NULL,'GHBC-C-007198','Buildings certified at design and construction stage with any of the international green building certification systems (EDGE, DGNB, LEED, BREEAM, Green Star or any other government approved rating system) shall be considered as a replacement to all prescriptive requirements of this Code.','approval',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','5f6748503fb95f31949630a2a4a04277d5a9b4680d2ec3905b91cf2bd77c6ec2','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26325','GHBC-REQ-026325','GS 1207:2018',37,'37.10',NULL,'GHBC-C-007198','Project owners must submit the design certificate for one of the above-mentioned certification systems to be eligible to receive the Building Permit.','approval',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a91c03c22470e6d0c8221df1c17c20acd224389be67d110a16f0707d8e333c88','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26326','GHBC-REQ-026326','GS 1207:2018',37,'37.10',NULL,'GHBC-C-007198','To get the Certificate of Habitation, the project owner needs to provide either the final certificate from the above-mentioned systems, OR arrange for an accredited 3rd party inspector to conduct a site visit and issue a report of compliance with the respective certification requirements.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','a32d1f81faddcf9c742263112f83a94a4ae09273c3a2d4c2cfa515a26dc9be2e','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26327','GHBC-REQ-026327','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007199','2.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["Within flood hazard areas, historic structures that do not meet one or more of the following designations: 1. Listed or preliminarily determined to be eligible for listing in the National Register of Historic Places.","Where such equipment and appliances are designed and installed to prevent water from entering or accumulating within their components and the systems are constructed to resist hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and stresses, including the effects of buoyancy, during the occurrence of flooding up to the elevation required by this Code. The systems and equipment shall be permitted to be located below the elevation required by this Code. Electrical wiring systems shall be permitted below the design","Electrical systems, equipment and components; heating, ventilating, air conditioning and plumbing appliances; plumbing fixtures, duct systems and other service equipment shall be permitted to be","Signs on flat roofs with every part of the roof accessible. E.10.2 Bearing plates. The bearing plates of roof signs shall distribute the load directly to or on masonry walls, steel roof girders, columns or beams. The building shall be designed to avoid overstress of these members."]','[]','["GS 1009"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','762ae15ada61abd6979692b93dc129aadefb2e03b7a1a82623249adea9c25df9','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26328','GHBC-REQ-026328','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007199','Determined by the appropriate government agency as contributing to the historical significance.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["Within flood hazard areas, historic structures that do not meet one or more of the following designations: 1. Listed or preliminarily determined to be eligible for listing in the National Register of Historic Places.","Where such equipment and appliances are designed and installed to prevent water from entering or accumulating within their components and the systems are constructed to resist hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and stresses, including the effects of buoyancy, during the occurrence of flooding up to the elevation required by this Code. The systems and equipment shall be permitted to be located below the elevation required by this Code. Electrical wiring systems shall be permitted below the design","Electrical systems, equipment and components; heating, ventilating, air conditioning and plumbing appliances; plumbing fixtures, duct systems and other service equipment shall be permitted to be","Signs on flat roofs with every part of the roof accessible. E.10.2 Bearing plates. The bearing plates of roof signs shall distribute the load directly to or on masonry walls, steel roof girders, columns or beams. The building shall be designed to avoid overstress of these members."]','[]','["GS 1009"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','681806f55f025072378162f86b70301cd836211b16a334d9c02d6d42dab3dea5','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26329','GHBC-REQ-026329','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007199','3.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["Within flood hazard areas, historic structures that do not meet one or more of the following designations: 1. Listed or preliminarily determined to be eligible for listing in the National Register of Historic Places.","Where such equipment and appliances are designed and installed to prevent water from entering or accumulating within their components and the systems are constructed to resist hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and stresses, including the effects of buoyancy, during the occurrence of flooding up to the elevation required by this Code. The systems and equipment shall be permitted to be located below the elevation required by this Code. Electrical wiring systems shall be permitted below the design","Electrical systems, equipment and components; heating, ventilating, air conditioning and plumbing appliances; plumbing fixtures, duct systems and other service equipment shall be permitted to be","Signs on flat roofs with every part of the roof accessible. E.10.2 Bearing plates. The bearing plates of roof signs shall distribute the load directly to or on masonry walls, steel roof girders, columns or beams. The building shall be designed to avoid overstress of these members."]','[]','["GS 1009"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','af22d7328ee79e21c5835d1bb7528562ab5a8e856cb2d98ff12837f4d63d720f','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26330','GHBC-REQ-026330','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007199','Designated as historic under a national or local historic preservation program that is approved by the Department of Interior.','approval',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["Within flood hazard areas, historic structures that do not meet one or more of the following designations: 1. Listed or preliminarily determined to be eligible for listing in the National Register of Historic Places.","Where such equipment and appliances are designed and installed to prevent water from entering or accumulating within their components and the systems are constructed to resist hydrostatic and hydrodynamic loads and stresses, including the effects of buoyancy, during the occurrence of flooding up to the elevation required by this Code. The systems and equipment shall be permitted to be located below the elevation required by this Code. Electrical wiring systems shall be permitted below the design","Electrical systems, equipment and components; heating, ventilating, air conditioning and plumbing appliances; plumbing fixtures, duct systems and other service equipment shall be permitted to be","Signs on flat roofs with every part of the roof accessible. E.10.2 Bearing plates. The bearing plates of roof signs shall distribute the load directly to or on masonry walls, steel roof girders, columns or beams. The building shall be designed to avoid overstress of these members."]','[]','["GS 1009"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','6dee9604404f8409f5eb2566711f00e9781a155edb028f53cd320095b6f42464','2026-08-15 13:56:14');
