('rowid-26888','GHBC-REQ-026888','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrodynamic loads are generally lateral forces, but   also include effects of the turbulence resulting from the interaction of the flowing water   mass with a rigid structure.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','c82872953f49bb457c1037ba0fbfd0e801e64a3a6f9b1984d41ced0146540c8d','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26889','GHBC-REQ-026889','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrodynamic load computations for construction consider all predominant forcing functions responsible for the motion of the aquatic mass, which are the   astronomical tide and the storm waves (including   the orbital particle transport, longshore   mass transport, and shore-normal mass transport), as well as  the storm surge.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','eb0327a21e842e854085f18ac3f7a3136c69037a0f0336d71f355bfa1d2d89c1','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26890','GHBC-REQ-026890','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Gravity and forced flow resulting from the inundation accompanying the storm surge of a I DO-year storm event are considered.','informational',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','fc900f31ba4238ec956c72de5e12332a45077187638369a2ec115d9a21a81fbf','2026-08-15 13:56:14');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO "requirements" ("id", "requirement_id", "source_document", "part", "section", "clause", "clause_id", "source_text", "requirement_type", "subject", "condition", "action", "object", "exceptions", "parameters_json", "references_json", "confidence", "verification_status", "editorial_state", "effective_date", "content_hash", "created_at") VALUES ('rowid-26891','GHBC-REQ-026891','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrodynamic load computations consider the processes of mass transport, heat transport, and momentum transport, along with the corresponding  natural laws which are the conservation of matter, the conservation of energy (first law of   thermodynamics), and Newton''s second law (the equation of motion).','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','ec7661dd79fa97b29ffdd7f5097dcf978eb201c199df201c2b694e008e6afa8b','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26892','GHBC-REQ-026892','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrodynamic load   computations also consider the various flow forms including forms referring to spatial variation   (uniform and nonuniform flow), forms referring to variation in time (steady, quasi-steady, and non-steady flow), forms referring to the nature of flow (laminar and turbulent flow), and forms referring to the type of flow energy (subcritical, critical, and supercritical flow).','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','f17ad1471555033eef9123d82d0543005b7e8c5ce1f4ba4fe64ae2aa0aa8dc83','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26893','GHBC-REQ-026893','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','In addition,   hydrodynamic load computations include the transformation of flow energy form from   supercritical flow to subcritical flow, and vice versa, including all classifications of hydraulic jump.','energy',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','379aae1066292f97acd27171b4d81c1fa5771d6a7f999ff2ee0946d4f7fc441e','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26894','GHBC-REQ-026894','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrodynamic load computations consider hydraulic flow across both a fixed bed and    a movable bed where applicable.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','1107b2345c8e276eed0201cfcc64fbbdc354a4be8c730587060a0659730752aa','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26895','GHBC-REQ-026895','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','DGS 1207: 2018 HYDROSTATIC LOADS: Those lateral and vertical (including uplift) forces resulting from a mass of water standing either above or below the soil surface.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[{"parameter":"measurement","value":2018,"unit":"h","operator":null,"context":"DGS 1207: 2018 HYDROSTATIC LOADS: Those latera"}]','["is1"]',0.93,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','c91254e89a83fbbe59bc6dc916ab11258907cb5d74f6cb84f9c300959602d916','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26896','GHBC-REQ-026896','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','These loads are equal to the product of the water pressure at the centroid of the plane surface area on which the   pressure acts times the area of that surface.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','53b829a2b62164f955396e255d59090b90202b20d1adbdfd225b3f612d5bb210','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26897','GHBC-REQ-026897','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','The hydrostatic pressure is equal to the  product of the  unit   weight  of  the  water  times  the elevation  of  the water  above the  point  of measurement.','mechanical',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','5975098bf51900626cd5059e9bbb890772ac87031a784c50c486fc5d618521eb','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
