('rowid-26952','GHBC-REQ-026952','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Design wave loading analysis should consider vertical uplift pressures and all lateral pressures to include impact, as well as, dynamic loading and   the harmonic intensification resulting from repetitive waves.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','fd1d06563769a4debd4809c38bdb62d3533158acfca1eb65b3e76e74e18a23f9','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26953','GHBC-REQ-026953','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','In addition to the wind and wave loads, a coastal building Code should require that all major habitable structures  be  designed for the hydrostatic and hydrodynamic  loads which would be  expected  under  the  conditions  of maximum inundation  associated with a  I00year storm event.Calculations for hydrostatic loads should  consider the maximum  water pressure resulting from  a  peaked  breaking wave superimposed on the  storm  surge of  a I00- year storm event.','mandatory',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','408d66c83f3380f0f9812f0de2817c6b4991ea8b58e735eefa4f10e3bd4ee458','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26954','GHBC-REQ-026954','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Both free and confined hydrostatic loads should be considered, while confined hydrostatic loads should be determined using the maximum elevation to which the confined water would freely rise if unconfined.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','5bc9e2a2a4ea6e761b108b05f89850f579b26d5c993e34e8b61dad9e0acfe5fa','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26955','GHBC-REQ-026955','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Vertical hydrostatic loads should be considered as forces acting both vertically downward and upward on horizontal or inclined surfaces of major structures (e.g. floors, slabs, roofs,   walls).','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','b5fb3a69b0bede74bae89401e8dff3295f149cae4027bd0f96214eae00a241b5','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26956','GHBC-REQ-026956','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Lateral hydrostatic loads should be considered as forces acting horizontally above and below grade on vertical or inclined surfaces of major structures and coastal or shore protection structures.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','79470f9abf1f54c1b06ef7c4200395c40e580cf4bb721725bc8a1caed928aee4','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
('rowid-26957','GHBC-REQ-026957','GS 1207:2018',38,NULL,NULL,'GHBC-C-007201','Hydrostatic loads on irregular or curving geometric surfaces may be determined in consideration of separate vertical and horizontal components acting simultaneously under the distribution of the hydrostatic pressures.','dimensional',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'["A geotechnical report is not required where the head of the works department determines that the nature of the work applied for is such that a report is not necessary.","A liquefaction study is not required where the head of the works department determines from established local data that the liquefaction potential is low.","Drainage facilities and terracing need not be provided where the ground slope is not steeper than one unit vertical in three units horizontal (33-percent slope). G1.9.2 Terraces. Terraces not less than 1829 mm (6 feet) in width shall be established at not more than 9144 mm (30-foot) vertical intervals on all cut or fill slopes to control surface drainage and debris. Suitable access shall be provided to allow for cleaning and maintenance.","Erosion control measures need not be provided on cut slopes not subject to erosion due to the erosion-resistant character of the materials. Erosion control for the slopes shall be installed as soon as practicable and prior to calling for final inspection."]','[]','["is1"]',0.9,'requires_review','DRAFT','2018','3e3a30e6ea1afe841748ca7a602503fec43d37182da95adebed4a0834650cf94','2026-08-15 13:56:14'),
